                        <p class="text-slate-600 text-lg mb-6">
                            The system requires high torque to curl the 20-unit assembly. A custom housing manages the electronics and provides a rigid base for the actuation system.
                        </p>
                        <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
                            <li class="bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-100">
                                <span class="block font-bold text-blue-800 mb-1">Actuator</span>
                                <span class="text-sm text-slate-600">55kg-cm Brushless Continuous Rotation Servo acting as a winch.</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-100">
                                <span class="block font-bold text-blue-800 mb-1">Microcontroller</span>
                                <span class="text-sm text-slate-600">Arduino R4 WiFi handling logic and state management.</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-100">
                                <span class="block font-bold text-blue-800 mb-1">Power</span>
                                <span class="text-sm text-slate-600">Dedicated 5V 15A PSU to isolate high-current motor loads.</span>
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Software -->
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Control Logic</h3>
                        <p class="text-slate-600 text-lg mb-6">
                            Since continuous rotation servos lack position feedback, the control system implements a state machine with a custom Processing interface for real-time safety.
                        </p>
                        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-6 font-mono text-sm text-blue-300 overflow-x-auto shadow-lg">
                            <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-4 border-b border-slate-700 pb-2">
                                <span class="text-slate-400">Arduino Control Snippet</span>
                                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500">C++</span>
                            </div>
<pre><code>// State Machine for Winch Control
if (command == 'F') {
    // Curl: Spin forward to pull cable
    motorA.writeMicroseconds(1550); 
} 
else if (command == 'B') {
    // Release: Spin backward to release tension
    motorA.writeMicroseconds(1450); 
} 
else if (command == 'S') {
    // Hold: Stop spinning to maintain grasp
    motorA.writeMicroseconds(1500); 
}</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Section: Challenges -->
