                         <!-- Challenge 1 -->
                         <div class="border border-slate-200 p-6 rounded-xl hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                             <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-red-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-red-500 mb-4">
                                 <i class="fas fa-arrow-up text-xl"></i>
                             </div>
                             <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">The "Lifting" Issue</h3>
                             <p class="text-slate-600">
                                 Initial tests showed the winch pulling the entire arm upwards bodily due to friction, rather than curling it. 
                                 <br><br>
                                 <strong>Solution:</strong> A custom housing was designed to rigidly hold all components relative to the base, blocking the arm's vertical translation and forcing the energy into the curling motion.
                             </p>
                         </div>
                         <!-- Challenge 2 -->
                         <div class="border border-slate-200 p-6 rounded-xl hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                             <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-orange-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-orange-500 mb-4">
                                 <i class="fas fa-cog text-xl"></i>
                             </div>
                             <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Winch Slip & Torque</h3>
                             <p class="text-slate-600">
                                 The 55kg-cm torque stripped the plastic-on-metal press fit of the custom PLA winch.
                                 <br><br>
                                 <strong>Solution:</strong> A reinforced mounting solution using zip-ties was implemented to mechanically bind the spool to the servo horn, preventing rotation slippage without requiring machined metal parts.
                             </p>
                         </div>
                     </div>
                </section>

